[{"answer":"For my presentation today","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/1.mp3"},{"answer":"I want to tell you about how groups of elephants have been moved and settled in new reserves.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/2.mp3"},{"answer":"This is known as translocation and has been carried out in Malawi in Africa in recent years.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/3.mp3"},{"answer":"The reason this is being done is because of overpopulation of elephants in some areas.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/4.mp3"},{"answer":"Overpopulation is a good problem to have","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/5.mp3"},{"answer":"and not one we tend to hear about very often.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/6.mp3"},{"answer":"In Malawi's Majete National Park","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/7.mp3"},{"answer":"the elephant population had been wiped out by poachers,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/8.mp3"},{"answer":"who killed the elephants for their ivory.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/9.mp3"},{"answer":"But in 2003,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/10.mp3"},{"answer":"the park was restocked and effective law enforcement was introduced.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/11.mp3"},{"answer":"Since then, not a single elephant has been poached.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/12.mp3"},{"answer":"In this safe environment, the elephant population boomed.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/13.mp3"},{"answer":"Breeding went so well that there were more elephants than the park could support.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/14.mp3"},{"answer":"This led to a number of problems.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/15.mp3"},{"answer":"Firstly, there was more competition for food,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/16.mp3"},{"answer":"which meant that some elephants were suffering from hunger.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/17.mp3"},{"answer":"As there was a limit to the amount of food in the national park,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/18.mp3"},{"answer":"some elephants began looking further afield.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/19.mp3"},{"answer":"Elephants were routinely knocking down fences around the park,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/20.mp3"},{"answer":"which then had to be repaired at a significant cost.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/21.mp3"},{"answer":"To solve this problem,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/22.mp3"},{"answer":"the decision was made to move dozens of elephants from Majete National Park to Nkhotakota Wildlife Park,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/23.mp3"},{"answer":"where there were no elephants.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/24.mp3"},{"answer":"But, obviously, attempting to move significant numbers of elephants to a new home 300 kilometres away is quite a challenge.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/25.mp3"},{"answer":"So how did this translocation process work in practice?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Elephants were moved in groups of between eight and twenty,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/27.mp3"},{"answer":"all belonging to one family.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/28.mp3"},{"answer":"Because relationships are very important to elephants,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/29.mp3"},{"answer":"they all had to be moved at the same time.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/30.mp3"},{"answer":"A team of vets and park rangers flew over the park in helicopters and targeted a group,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/31.mp3"},{"answer":"which were rounded up and directed to a designated open plain.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/32.mp3"},{"answer":"The vets then used darts to immobilise the elephants.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/33.mp3"},{"answer":"This was a tricky manoeuvre,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/34.mp3"},{"answer":"as they not only had to select the right dose of tranquiliser for different-sized elephants","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/35.mp3"},{"answer":"but they had to dart the elephants as they were running around.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/36.mp3"},{"answer":"This also had to be done as quickly as possible","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/37.mp3"},{"answer":"so as to minimise the stress caused.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/38.mp3"},{"answer":"As soon as the elephants began to flop onto the ground,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/39.mp3"},{"answer":"the team moved in to take care of them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/40.mp3"},{"answer":"To avoid the risk of suffocation,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/41.mp3"},{"answer":"the team had to make sure none of the elephants were lying on their chests","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/42.mp3"},{"answer":"because their lungs could be crushed in this position.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/43.mp3"},{"answer":"So all the elephants had to be placed on their sides.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/44.mp3"},{"answer":"One person stayed with each elephant","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/45.mp3"},{"answer":"while they waited for the vets to do checks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/46.mp3"},{"answer":"It was very important to keep an eye on their breathing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/47.mp3"},{"answer":"If there were fewer than six breaths per minute,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/48.mp3"},{"answer":"the elephant would need urgent medical attention.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/49.mp3"},{"answer":"Collars were fitted to the matriarch in each group","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/50.mp3"},{"answer":"so their movements could be tracked in their new home.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/51.mp3"},{"answer":"Measurements were taken of each elephant's tusks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/52.mp3"},{"answer":"Elephants with large tusks would be at greater risk from poachers","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/53.mp3"},{"answer":"and also of their feet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/54.mp3"},{"answer":"The elephants were then taken to a recovery area","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/55.mp3"},{"answer":"before being loaded onto trucks and transported to their new home.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/56.mp3"},{"answer":"The elephants translocated to Nkhotakota settled in very well","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/57.mp3"},{"answer":"and the project has generally been accepted to have been a huge success","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/58.mp3"},{"answer":"and not just for the elephants.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/59.mp3"},{"answer":"Employment prospects have improved enormously,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/60.mp3"},{"answer":"contributing to rising living standards for the whole community.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/61.mp3"},{"answer":"Poaching is no longer an issue,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/62.mp3"},{"answer":"as former poachers are able to find more reliable sources of income.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/63.mp3"},{"answer":"In fact, many of them volunteered to give up their weapons,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/64.mp3"},{"answer":"as they were no longer of any use to them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/65.mp3"},{"answer":"More than two dozen elephants have been born at Nkhotakota since relocation.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/66.mp3"},{"answer":"With an area of more than 1,800 square kilometres,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/67.mp3"},{"answer":"there's plenty of space for the elephant population to continue to grow.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/68.mp3"},{"answer":"Their presence is also helping to rebalance Nkhotakota's damaged ecosystem","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/69.mp3"},{"answer":"and providing a sustainable conservation model, which could be replicated in other parks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/70.mp3"},{"answer":"All this has been a big draw for tourism,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/71.mp3"},{"answer":"which contributes five times more than the illegal wildlife trade to GDP,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/72.mp3"},{"answer":"and this is mainly because of the elephants.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/73.mp3"},{"answer":"There's also been a dramatic rise...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-1-part-4-2023-06-16-20-38-26/74.mp3"}]
